module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.refined_alias_argument_exempt_from_declared_type_inhabitance

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data refined_alias_argument_exempt_from_declared_type_inhabitance: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "refined_alias_argument_exempt_from_declared_type_inhabitance" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "SUBJECT: a value whose type is a where-refined alias of a kernel primitive -- std.types FilePath, NonEmptyStr, any `String where ...` -- supplied at a direct-call argument position whose declared formal is a RECORD. The floor obligation is that values inhabit declared types (DESIGN 4b, the floor first); this is the floor broken for one argument shape.",
    "SPECIMEN, MEASURED THROUGH compile_dag_diagnostic_census ON THE INTERPRETATION PATH, 2026-09-13, at main b2f9a0c5bbe plus the change filing this row. Formal: `fn take(v: Wrapped) -> Int` with `type Wrapped sole_constructor { inner: ... }`, a monomorphic record. Four arguments, one term changed each time: a String LITERAL refuses (TypeMismatch|Primitive(String) and DeclaredTypeNotInhabited at the argument); a parameter typed String refuses the same way; a parameter typed Int refuses; a parameter typed FilePath is ADMITTED WITH NO ROW AT ALL -- no blocking diagnostic and no advisory names the argument -- and so is `\"x\" as FilePath`. The same four at a generic-instantiation formal (Sealed<JobLog, String>, directly or through an alias) admit the FilePath forms identically. A foreign record at the monomorphic formal refuses (DeclaredTypeNotInhabited), so the exemption is specific to refined-alias arguments, not to non-literal arguments.",
    "ENROLLED FORM: test.probe.durable_write_takes_the_value_probe hands gunbc.fabric_m0_origin_commit commit_object_to_origin a FilePath where its DataEffectPermit<BuildOutput, FilePath> is declared; test.claim.data_class_refusal_probe_witness the_durable_write_still_admits_a_file_path_where_the_permit_is_declared asserts the zero at that argument and flips red when the exemption closes, beside the_durable_write_refuses_a_bare_string_literal_where_the_permit_is_declared, the refusing control one term away.",
    "HARM: silent, not merely weak. The admitted call reaches the effect at run time with a String where a record is expected; the interpreter fails there untyped rather than the compiler refusing located. For the product carrier this is the class 'a durable write called with the value instead of the permit', which the permit-taking signature was built to make unwritable and which on this path it does not.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT AND CURRENT RUNG: silent acceptance, outside the ladder, on interpretation. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- the argument's type is a resolved alias of a kernel primitive and the formal is a resolved record; the mismatch is decidable from the two resolved heads, as the String-literal arm of the same specimen shows the checker already deciding. The emitted-Rust path is not measured for this class in the filing change.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, capability grain: the direct-call inhabitance judgment peels a where-refined alias to its base carrier before judging, so a refined alias value is judged exactly as its base primitive is at the same position -- refused at a record formal, admitted at its own alias or base. Sufficient for flipping the enrolled probe to ExpectBlockingRefusal. Not satisfied by judging literals only, nor by an advisory row at the position.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
